#: ../../../autoapi/gemm_relu/index.rst:8
msgid "Demo kernel for the pass visualizer: fused GEMM + bias + ReLU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/gemm_relu/index.rst:10
msgid "C = relu(A @ B + bias)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/gemm_relu/index.rst:12
msgid ""
"`bias` is a per-output-column vector of shape (N,), broadcast across rows. "
"Both the bias add and the ReLU are fused into the GEMM epilogue: they run on "
"the accumulator fragment `C_local` (still in registers) right before writing "
"back to global memory. No extra kernel launch, no extra global round-trip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/gemm_relu/index.rst:17
msgid ""
